#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Curtis Galloway
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
"""Sync agent state into the local filesystem based on a JSON manifest.

The sync has three parts:

  1. Generic (always): every `skills` entry — plus the skills discovered in
     each `skill_repos` checkout (a repo with a Claude Code
     .claude-plugin/marketplace.json is read plugin by plugin, optionally
     filtered to named plugins; otherwise its skills/ dir) — is symlinked
     into the agent-neutral skills directory ~/.agents/skills/ (override
     with --skills-target).
     `links` entries whose destination is outside a per-agent directory
     are also applied here.

  2. Claude Code (only if Claude is installed — `claude` on PATH or
     ~/.claude/ present): `links` entries with destinations under ~/.claude/
     (CLAUDE.md, hooks, ...) are applied, ~/.claude/skills is symlinked to
     the generic skills directory so Claude sees the same skill set, and the
     `claude_settings` policy fragments are MERGED into the app-owned
     ~/.claude/settings.json (see below). Then plugins are reconciled: any
     marketplace the merged policy names in `extraKnownMarketplaces` and
     any plugin it enables in `enabledPlugins` that is missing locally is
     registered/installed through the `claude plugin` CLI. If
     ~/.claude/skills is still a real directory from an older sync, it is
     converted automatically once stale symlinks are cleaned up.

  3. Antigravity (only if agy is installed — `agy` on PATH or
     ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/ present): `links` entries with destinations
     under ~/.gemini/ (AGENTS.md, ...) are applied,
     ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/skills is symlinked to the generic skills
     directory so agy sees the same skill set, and the `agy_settings`
     policy fragments are MERGED into the app-owned
     ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json. Same mechanism as Claude
     Code, same reasons.

A manifest is a JSON file at manifests/<name>.json with this shape:

    {
      "name": "laptop",
      "description": "...",
      "schema": 2,
      "skill_repos": [
        { "path": "${HOME}/src/public-skills" },
        { "path": "${HOME}/src/fuchsia-skills", "plugins": ["fuchsia-skills"] }
      ],
      "skills": [
        { "name": "learn", "path": "${QBRANCH_ROOT}/skills/learn" },
        { "name": "paniolo", "repo": "git@github.com:user/paniolo.git",
          "path": "skills/paniolo" }
      ],
      "links": [
        { "src": "${QBRANCH_ROOT}/claude-code/CLAUDE.md",
          "dst": "${HOME}/.claude/CLAUDE.md" },
        { "src": "${QBRANCH_ROOT}/claude-code/hooks/permission-notify.sh",
          "dst": "${HOME}/.claude/hooks/permission-notify.sh" },
        { "src": "${QBRANCH_ROOT}/agy/AGENTS.md",
          "dst": "${HOME}/.gemini/AGENTS.md" }
      ],
      "claude_settings": [
        "${QBRANCH_ROOT}/claude-code/settings.json",
        "${QBRANCH_ROOT}/claude-code/settings/hosts/laptop.json"
      ],
      "agy_settings": [
        "${QBRANCH_ROOT}/agy/settings.json"
      ]
    }

`skills` is shorthand for "link this into the skills target directory under
the entry's name". `links` is the general form: any source linked to any
destination — agent harness state (hooks, instruction files) or anything
else.

`skill_repos` lists checkouts whose skills are linked without per-skill
manifest entries. A repo with a Claude Code marketplace
(.claude-plugin/marketplace.json) contributes the skills each plugin entry
lists, so `"plugins": [...]` picks themes; a plain repo contributes
skills/*/SKILL.md. Manifest `skills` win on a name collision, then earlier
repos over later ones.

Manifests carry `"schema": N` (1 when absent). An older manifest is
upgraded in memory on every load and rewritten by --upgrade-manifests; a
newer one is refused with a pointer to update the tool. Forward-only, by
design, so a manifest never has to be edited by hand to keep working with
a newer tool.

`claude_settings` lists git-tracked policy fragments (shared base first,
host fragment after) that are merged in order — dicts recurse, lists union,
later scalars win — and then imposed on the live ~/.claude/settings.json.
That file is deliberately NOT a symlink: Claude Code rewrites it at will
(theme, effortLevel, enabledPlugins, notification prefs), so the app owns
the file and the sync owns only the policy keys inside it. Policy list
items are added if missing, policy scalars overwrite, app-owned keys are
untouched. The state file remembers the applied policy snapshot, so a key
removed from the fragments is retracted from the live file on the next
sync (unless the app changed its value in the meantime). Claude Code does
NOT read a user-level ~/.claude/settings.local.json (verified empirically,
v2.1.167) — that's why merging, not file-splitting, is used here.

Plugins ride on the same fragments. `extraKnownMarketplaces` names the
marketplaces to register and `enabledPlugins` (id -> true) the plugins to
install at user scope; after the merge, whatever is missing locally is
added via `claude plugin marketplace add` / `claude plugin install`. An
installed plugin with no enabledPlugins entry is disabled as far as Claude
Code is concerned, so a plugin dropped from the fragments is disabled by
the ordinary settings retraction and reported — never uninstalled, since
that would delete its data directory. A plugin is *managed* when a fragment
declares it (true or false) and *unmanaged* when it is installed locally but
declared nowhere; unmanaged plugins are reported, like skills missing from
the manifest, and otherwise left alone.

`agy_settings` is the same thing for Antigravity, targeting the app-owned
~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json. That file mixes policy (the
permission allowlist) with app state (theme), so it gets merged rather
than symlinked for the same reason.

Skills entries support two source forms:
  - path-based:  { "name": "...", "path": "<local-path>" }
  - repo-based:  { "name": "...", "repo": "<git-url>", "path": "<repo-relative-path>" }

For repo-based entries the script looks up ~/src/<repo-name> first (by
convention); if that directory is a git checkout it is used directly.
Otherwise the repo is cloned (and kept updated) under
~/.agents/skill-repos/<repo-name>/.

Both local path and dst fields support:
  - ${QBRANCH_ROOT}       (the config root)
  - any environment variable via ${VAR}
  - a leading ~

The config root is --root, else $QBRANCH_ROOT, else the root the last sync
remembered in the state file, else the current directory when it holds
manifests/. The manifest is --manifest, else the last synced one, else the
one named after this host, else `default`.

Links are symbolic links by default. `--link-mode copy` materialises every
entry as a copy instead (refreshed on each sync, removed when dropped), for
filesystems or Windows setups without symlinks; the default `auto` falls
back to copies on Windows when symlinks are unavailable. The choice is
remembered like --root; `--link-mode auto` forgets it.

The script:
  - Symlinks each entry into its destination, creating parent dirs as needed.
  - Refuses to overwrite a non-symlink at the destination.
  - Tracks every destination it created in
    <skills_target>/.qbranch-state.json so swapping manifests removes
    stale links (and copies) even when they pointed outside this repo.
  - Registers the marketplaces and installs the plugins the merged
    claude_settings policy declares, via the `claude plugin` CLI.
  - `--plugin-status [--json]` classifies this machine's plugins as
    managed / unmanaged / no longer managed; `--manage-plugin ID --in
    base|host [--value false]` declares one in a fragment. The
    review-plugins skill drives these two to triage unmanaged plugins.
  - `--dry-run --json` prints the plan as JSON: the actions, plugin
    actions and messages a sync would produce. tests/run_corpus.py
    compares it against the corpus under tests/corpus/, which is the
    specification a port of this tool has to satisfy.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from copy import deepcopy
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path

# The config root: manifests/, skills/ and claude-code/ live here. Set once
# per run by resolve_root() before anything reads it.
REPO = Path(".")
DEFAULT_SKILLS_TARGET = Path.home() / ".agents" / "skills"
STATE_FILE_NAME = ".qbranch-state.json"
LEGACY_STATE_FILE_NAME = ".agent-skills-state.json"
VERSION = "0.3.0"
# Manifests carry a `schema` (1 when absent). Older schemas are upgraded in
# memory on every load and rewritten by --upgrade-manifests; a manifest newer
# than MANIFEST_SCHEMA is refused, so the upgrade path is forward-only.
MANIFEST_SCHEMA = 2
STATE_SCHEMA = 2
# The tool's own skills, beside this script in a checkout. --skill prints
# them; the Rust port embeds the same files at build time.
BUNDLED_SKILLS_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "skills"
SKILL_REPOS_CACHE = Path.home() / ".agents" / "skill-repos"
# How a manifest entry is materialised: a symbolic link, or a copy that is
# refreshed on every sync. `auto` is symlink, falling back to copy on Windows
# when the process may not create links.
LINK_MODES = ("auto", "symlink", "copy")
# Never copied into a copy of a skills directory, and ignored when checking
# whether a copy is up to date.
COPY_IGNORE = {STATE_FILE_NAME, LEGACY_STATE_FILE_NAME}
# Claude Code relocates its whole config dir via CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR; honor it
# so a sync against a scratch config dir exercises the real code paths.
CLAUDE_DIR = Path(os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or Path.home() / ".claude")
CLAUDE_SKILLS_LINK = CLAUDE_DIR / "skills"
CLAUDE_SETTINGS_FILE = CLAUDE_DIR / "settings.json"
# User-scope MCP servers live in the app-owned ~/.claude.json, which moves
# into the config dir when CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is set. Read-only here.
CLAUDE_JSON_FILE = (CLAUDE_DIR / ".claude.json" if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR")
                    else Path.home() / ".claude.json")
# Antigravity keeps its harness state under ~/.gemini: instruction files at
# the top level, CLI-specific state (skills, settings) one level down.
AGY_DIR = Path.home() / ".gemini"
AGY_CLI_DIR = AGY_DIR / "antigravity-cli"
AGY_SKILLS_LINK = AGY_CLI_DIR / "skills"
AGY_SETTINGS_FILE = AGY_CLI_DIR / "settings.json"
# Claude Code registers its own marketplace on first interactive run, but the
# `claude plugin` CLI does not — on a fresh config dir it must be added like
# any other before an official plugin can be installed.
OFFICIAL_MARKETPLACE = "claude-plugins-official"
OFFICIAL_MARKETPLACE_SOURCE = {
    "source": {"source": "github", "repo": "anthropics/claude-plugins-official"}
}


def expand_path(raw: str) -> Path:
    s = raw.replace("${QBRANCH_ROOT}", str(REPO))
    s = os.path.expandvars(s)
    return Path(s).expanduser()


def claude_installed() -> bool:
    return shutil.which("claude") is not None or CLAUDE_DIR.is_dir()


def agy_installed() -> bool:
    return shutil.which("agy") is not None or AGY_CLI_DIR.is_dir()


def is_under(p: Path, root: Path) -> bool:
    try:
        p.relative_to(root)
        return True
    except ValueError:
        return False


def repo_name_from_url(url: str) -> str:
    """Extract 'paniolo' from 'git@github.com:user/paniolo.git'."""
    name = url.rstrip("/").split("/")[-1]
    if name.endswith(".git"):
        name = name[:-4]
    return name


def resolve_repo_local(repo_url: str) -> Path:
    """Return the local root of repo_url, cloning if necessary.

    Checks ~/src/<name> first (convention); if that's a git checkout it is
    used as-is. Otherwise clones into ~/.agents/skill-repos/<name>/ and pulls
    on every subsequent sync.
    """
    name = repo_name_from_url(repo_url)

    local = Path.home() / "src" / name
    if local.is_dir() and (local / ".git").exists():
        return local

    cache = SKILL_REPOS_CACHE / name
    if cache.is_dir() and (cache / ".git").exists():
        result = subprocess.run(
            ["git", "-C", str(cache), "pull", "--ff-only"],
            capture_output=True, text=True,
        )
        if result.returncode != 0:
            print(f"warning: git pull failed for {name}: {result.stderr.strip()}",
                  file=sys.stderr)
    else:
        SKILL_REPOS_CACHE.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        subprocess.run(["git", "clone", repo_url, str(cache)], check=True)
    return cache


def resolve_skill_src(entry: dict) -> Path:
    """Return the source Path for a skills entry (path-based or repo-based)."""
    if "repo" in entry:
        return resolve_repo_local(entry["repo"]) / entry["path"]
    return expand_path(entry["path"])


def parse_git_skill_url(arg: str) -> tuple[str, str, str]:
    """Parse a git:// shorthand → (skill_name, repo_url, skill_path).

    Two forms:
      Short:  git://<local-name>[/<path>]
        First segment has no dot → look up ~/src/<name> for the remote URL.
        git://paniolo/skills/paniolo
          → name=paniolo  repo=<origin of ~/src/paniolo>  path=skills/paniolo

      Full:   git://<host>/<owner>/<repo>[/<path>]
        First segment contains a dot → construct git@host:owner/repo.git.
        git://github.com/user/paniolo/skills/hdmicap
          → name=hdmicap  repo=git@github.com:user/paniolo.git  path=skills/hdmicap
    """
    rest = arg[len("git://"):]
    parts = rest.split("/")

    if "." not in parts[0]:
        repo_name = parts[0]
        path_parts = parts[1:]
        local = Path.home() / "src" / repo_name
        if not local.is_dir() or not (local / ".git").exists():
            sys.exit(
                f"git:// short form: ~/src/{repo_name} not found or not a git repo\n"
                f"use full form: git://<host>/<owner>/<repo>[/<path>]"
            )
        result = subprocess.run(
            ["git", "-C", str(local), "remote", "get-url", "origin"],
            capture_output=True, text=True,
        )
        if result.returncode != 0:
            sys.exit(f"could not get remote URL for ~/src/{repo_name}: {result.stderr.strip()}")
        repo_url = result.stdout.strip()
        skill_path = "/".join(path_parts) if path_parts else f"skills/{repo_name}"
        skill_name = path_parts[-1] if path_parts else repo_name
        return skill_name, repo_url, skill_path

    if len(parts) < 3:
        sys.exit(
            f"invalid git:// skill URL: {arg!r}\n"
            f"expected: git://<host>/<owner>/<repo>[/<path/to/skill>]"
        )
    host, owner, repo_part = parts[0], parts[1], parts[2]
    path_parts = parts[3:]
    repo_name = repo_part[:-4] if repo_part.endswith(".git") else repo_part
    repo_url = f"git@{host}:{owner}/{repo_name}.git"
    skill_path = "/".join(path_parts) if path_parts else f"skills/{repo_name}"
    skill_name = path_parts[-1] if path_parts else repo_name
    return skill_name, repo_url, skill_path


def migrate_manifest(name: str, m: dict) -> tuple[dict, list[str]]:
    """Upgrade a manifest dict to MANIFEST_SCHEMA in memory.

    Returns (manifest, notes) where notes describe each step taken. Exits
    on a manifest newer than this tool understands: the upgrade path is
    forward-only, so the fix is a newer tool, never a hand-edited manifest.
    """
    v = m.get("schema", 1)
    if not isinstance(v, int) or v > MANIFEST_SCHEMA:
        sys.exit(f"manifest '{name}' is schema {v}; qbranch {VERSION} "
                 f"understands up to schema {MANIFEST_SCHEMA} — update the tool")
    notes: list[str] = []
    if v < 2:
        m.setdefault("skill_repos", [])
        notes.append("schema 1 -> 2: skill_repos added (empty); list the "
                     "checkouts whose skills should be linked in bulk")
    if notes:
        m = {"schema": MANIFEST_SCHEMA,
             **{k: val for k, val in m.items() if k != "schema"}}
    return m, notes


def load_manifest(name: str) -> tuple[dict, list[str]]:
    """Load manifests/<name>.json upgraded to the current schema.

    Returns (manifest, upgrade_notes); notes are empty for a current one.
    """
    p = REPO / "manifests" / f"{name}.json"
    if not p.exists():
        sys.exit(f"manifest not found: {p}\n"
                 f"available: {', '.join(list_manifests()) or '(none)'}")
    return migrate_manifest(name, json.loads(p.read_text()))


def upgrade_manifests() -> int:
    """Rewrite every manifest at MANIFEST_SCHEMA. Never downgrades."""
    for name in list_manifests():
        p = REPO / "manifests" / f"{name}.json"
        raw = json.loads(p.read_text())
        before = json.dumps(raw, sort_keys=True)
        upgraded, notes = migrate_manifest(name, raw)
        if json.dumps(upgraded, sort_keys=True) == before:
            print(f"  up to date  {name} (schema {upgraded.get('schema', 1)})")
            continue
        p.write_text(json.dumps(upgraded, indent=2) + "\n")
        print(f"  upgraded    {name}: " + "; ".join(notes))
    print("\nCommit the rewritten manifests. A qbranch older than the "
          "schema they now carry refuses them.")
    return 0


def list_manifests() -> list[str]:
    d = REPO / "manifests"
    return sorted(p.stem for p in d.glob("*.json")) if d.is_dir() else []


def bundled_skills() -> list[str]:
    """Names of the skills that ship with the tool, sorted."""
    d = BUNDLED_SKILLS_DIR
    if not d.is_dir():
        return []
    return sorted(p.name for p in d.iterdir() if (p / "SKILL.md").is_file())


def print_skill(name: str) -> int:
    """--skill: list the bundled skills, or print one's SKILL.md verbatim."""
    names = bundled_skills()
    if not name:
        for n in names:
            print(n)
        return 0
    if name not in names:
        sys.exit(f"no bundled skill '{name}'; available: {', '.join(names)}")
    text = (BUNDLED_SKILLS_DIR / name / "SKILL.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    print(text, end="")
    return 0


def empty_state() -> dict:
    return {"manifest": None, "links": [], "copies": []}


def load_state(state_path: Path) -> dict:
    """Load sync state; an older sync's .agent-skills-state.json beside it counts."""
    if not state_path.exists():
        legacy = state_path.parent / LEGACY_STATE_FILE_NAME
        if legacy.is_file():
            state_path = legacy
    if not state_path.exists():
        return empty_state()
    try:
        data = json.loads(state_path.read_text())
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        return empty_state()
    if data.get("schema", 1) > STATE_SCHEMA:
        sys.exit(f"{state_path} was written by a newer qbranch "
                 f"(state schema {data['schema']}, this tool: {STATE_SCHEMA}) "
                 f"— update the tool")
    data.setdefault("links", [])
    data.setdefault("copies", [])
    return data


def resolve_root(explicit: str | None, state: dict) -> None:
    """Pick the config root for this run and store it in REPO.

    --root wins, then $QBRANCH_ROOT, then the root the last sync remembered
    in the state file, then the current directory when it holds manifests/.
    A root given explicitly must hold manifests/; a remembered one that no
    longer does is skipped.
    """
    candidates: list[tuple[str, Path]] = []
    if explicit:
        candidates.append(("--root", Path(explicit)))
    if os.environ.get("QBRANCH_ROOT"):
        candidates.append(("QBRANCH_ROOT", Path(os.environ["QBRANCH_ROOT"])))
    if state.get("root"):
        candidates.append(("remembered", Path(state["root"])))
    candidates.append(("cwd", Path.cwd()))
    for how, raw in candidates:
        p = raw.expanduser().resolve()
        if (p / "manifests").is_dir():
            globals()["REPO"] = p
            return
        if how in ("--root", "QBRANCH_ROOT"):
            sys.exit(f"no manifests/ under {p} ({how})")
    sys.exit("no config root: pass --root <dir> (remembered afterwards), set "
             "QBRANCH_ROOT, or run from a directory that holds manifests/")


def short_hostname() -> str:
    """This machine's name as a manifest name: the first label, lowercased."""
    return socket.gethostname().split(".")[0].lower()


def choose_manifest(explicit: str | None, state: dict) -> str:
    """--manifest, else the last synced one, else this host's, else `default`."""
    if explicit:
        return explicit
    if state.get("manifest"):
        return state["manifest"]
    available = list_manifests()
    for candidate in (short_hostname(), "default"):
        if candidate in available:
            return candidate
    sys.exit("no manifest chosen: pass --manifest <name> (remembered "
             f"afterwards); available: {', '.join(available) or '(none)'}")


def symlinks_available() -> bool:
    """Whether this process may create symbolic links (a Windows privilege)."""
    probe = Path(tempfile.gettempdir()) / f".qbranch-probe-{os.getpid()}"
    try:
        probe.symlink_to("qbranch-probe-target")
    except OSError:
        return False
    probe.unlink()
    return True


def decide_link_mode(
    requested: str | None, state: dict, notes: list[str]
) -> tuple[str, str | None]:
    """The link mode for this run, and the choice to remember.

    --link-mode (or $QBRANCH_LINK_MODE) wins and is remembered; `auto`
    forgets a remembered choice. Otherwise the remembered choice applies,
    else auto: symlinks, falling back to copies on Windows when the process
    may not create them.
    """
    chosen = requested or os.environ.get("QBRANCH_LINK_MODE") or None
    if chosen is not None and chosen not in LINK_MODES:
        sys.exit(f"--link-mode must be one of {', '.join(LINK_MODES)}, "
                 f"not '{chosen}'")
    remembered = state.get("link_mode")
    if remembered not in ("symlink", "copy"):
        remembered = None
    if chosen is None:
        chosen = remembered or "auto"
    elif chosen == "auto":
        remembered = None
    else:
        remembered = chosen
    if chosen != "auto":
        return chosen, remembered
    if os.name == "nt" and not symlinks_available():
        notes.append("symbolic links are unavailable here (on Windows, enable "
                     "Developer Mode to use them) — copying instead; "
                     "--link-mode symlink insists on links")
        return "copy", remembered
    return "symlink", remembered


def remove_path(p: Path) -> None:
    """Remove a link, a file or a whole directory tree at p."""
    if p.is_symlink() or p.is_file():
        p.unlink()
    elif p.is_dir():
        shutil.rmtree(p)


def copy_path(src: Path, dst: Path) -> None:
    """Copy src to dst (a directory tree or one file), replacing what is there.

    Symlinks inside src are followed, so the copy stands on its own; the
    state file is left out of a copied skills directory.
    """
    remove_path(dst)
    dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    if src.is_dir():
        shutil.copytree(
            src, dst, symlinks=False,
            ignore=lambda _d, names: [n for n in names if n in COPY_IGNORE])
    else:
        shutil.copy(src, dst)


def copy_up_to_date(src: Path, dst: Path) -> bool:
    """Whether dst is a faithful copy of src: same tree, same bytes."""
    if dst.is_symlink():
        return False
    if src.is_dir():
        return dst.is_dir() and trees_equal(src, dst)
    return dst.is_file() and src.read_bytes() == dst.read_bytes()


def trees_equal(a: Path, b: Path) -> bool:
    names_a = sorted(n.name for n in a.iterdir() if n.name not in COPY_IGNORE)
    names_b = sorted(n.name for n in b.iterdir() if n.name not in COPY_IGNORE)
    if names_a != names_b:
        return False
    for n in names_a:
        pa, pb = a / n, b / n
        if pb.is_symlink():
            return False
        if pa.is_dir():
            if not pb.is_dir() or not trees_equal(pa, pb):
                return False
        elif not pb.is_file() or pa.read_bytes() != pb.read_bytes():
            return False
    return True


def save_state(state_path: Path, manifest_name: str, links: list[Path],
               copies: list[Path], link_mode: str | None,
               settings_applied: dict[str, dict]) -> None:
    """Write the state file. `settings_applied` maps state key -> policy."""
    state_path.write_text(json.dumps({
        "schema": STATE_SCHEMA,
        "manifest": manifest_name,
        "root": str(REPO),
        "link_mode": link_mode,
        "linked_at": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
        "links": sorted({str(p) for p in links}),
        "copies": sorted({str(p) for p in copies}),
        **{k: v or {} for k, v in sorted(settings_applied.items())},
    }, indent=2) + "\n")
    legacy = state_path.parent / LEGACY_STATE_FILE_NAME
    if legacy.is_file():
        legacy.unlink()


def collect_desired(
    manifest: dict, skills_target: Path, claude_ok: bool, agy_ok: bool
) -> tuple[list[tuple[str, Path, Path]], list[str]]:
    """Return ((label, src, dst) tuples, skipped-entry notes) from the manifest."""
    out: list[tuple[str, Path, Path]] = []
    skipped: list[str] = []
    seen: set[Path] = set()

    for entry in manifest.get("skills", []):
        name = entry["name"]
        src = resolve_skill_src(entry)
        dst = skills_target / name
        if dst in seen:
            sys.exit(f"duplicate destination in manifest: {dst}")
        seen.add(dst)
        out.append((name, src, dst))

    for entry in manifest.get("links", []):
        src = expand_path(entry["src"])
        dst = expand_path(entry["dst"])
        label = entry.get("label") or dst.name
        if not claude_ok and is_under(dst, CLAUDE_DIR):
            skipped.append(f"{label}: {dst} (Claude Code not installed)")
            continue
        if not agy_ok and is_under(dst, AGY_DIR):
            skipped.append(f"{label}: {dst} (Antigravity not installed)")
            continue
        if dst in seen:
            sys.exit(f"duplicate destination in manifest: {dst}")
        seen.add(dst)
        out.append((label, src, dst))

    # Claude reads skills from ~/.claude/skills — point it at the generic dir.
    if claude_ok and CLAUDE_SKILLS_LINK != skills_target:
        out.append(("claude-skills", skills_target, CLAUDE_SKILLS_LINK))

    # Same for agy, which reads ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/skills.
    if agy_ok and AGY_SKILLS_LINK != skills_target:
        out.append(("agy-skills", skills_target, AGY_SKILLS_LINK))

    return out, skipped


def scan_skill_dirs(d: Path) -> list[Path]:
    """Immediate subdirectories of d that hold a SKILL.md, sorted."""
    if not d.is_dir():
        return []
    return [c for c in sorted(d.iterdir())
            if c.is_dir() and (c / "SKILL.md").is_file()]


def read_marketplace(repo: Path) -> dict | None:
    p = repo / ".claude-plugin" / "marketplace.json"
    if not p.is_file():
        return None
    try:
        return json.loads(p.read_text())
    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
        print(f"warning: {p}: {e} — treating {repo.name} as a plain skill repo",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return None


def repo_skill_dirs(
    repo: Path, only_plugins: list[str] | None
) -> tuple[list[tuple[Path, str]], str, list[str]]:
    """The skill directories a checkout offers, as (dir, plugin_name) pairs.

    A repo with .claude-plugin/marketplace.json is read the way Claude Code
    reads it: each plugin entry with a relative source contributes the
    skills paths it lists (a listed directory of skills is scanned, a listed
    skill is taken as-is) or, listing none, its whole skills/ folder.
    `only_plugins` narrows that to named entries. A repo without a
    marketplace contributes skills/*/SKILL.md. Also returns the marketplace
    name ("" for a plain repo) and warnings.
    """
    warnings: list[str] = []
    mkt = read_marketplace(repo)
    if mkt is None:
        if only_plugins:
            warnings.append(f"{repo.name}: no marketplace.json, so the "
                            f"'plugins' filter ({', '.join(map(str, only_plugins))}) "
                            f"is ignored")
        return [(d, "") for d in scan_skill_dirs(repo / "skills")], "", warnings

    entries = [e for e in (mkt.get("plugins") or []) if isinstance(e, dict)]
    if only_plugins:
        names = {e.get("name") for e in entries}
        for want in only_plugins:
            if want not in names:
                warnings.append(f"{repo.name}: marketplace has no plugin '{want}'")
        entries = [e for e in entries if e.get("name") in only_plugins]

    out: list[tuple[Path, str]] = []
    seen: set[Path] = set()
    for e in entries:
        src = e.get("source")
        if not isinstance(src, str) or not src.startswith("./"):
            continue  # a remote plugin source is not part of this checkout
        root = (repo / src).resolve()
        listed = e.get("skills")
        if listed:
            candidates: list[Path] = []
            for s in listed:
                d = (root / s).resolve()
                if (d / "SKILL.md").is_file():
                    candidates.append(d)
                elif d.is_dir():
                    candidates.extend(scan_skill_dirs(d))
                else:
                    warnings.append(f"{repo.name}/{e.get('name')}: listed "
                                    f"skill path missing: {d}")
        else:
            candidates = scan_skill_dirs(root / "skills")
        for d in candidates:
            if d in seen:
                continue
            seen.add(d)
            out.append((d, e.get("name") or ""))
    return out, mkt.get("name") or repo.name, warnings


def collect_repo_skills(
    manifest: dict, skills_target: Path, taken_dsts: set[Path]
) -> tuple[list[tuple[str, Path, Path]], list[str], list[Path],
           set[tuple[str, str]], dict[Path, str]]:
    """Implicit skill entries from every `skill_repos` checkout.

    Returns (entries, warnings, missing_repos, discovered, origins).
    `discovered` holds (marketplace, plugin) pairs whose skills were taken
    from a checkout — the plugin-install path would load those twice.
    `origins` maps each dst to "<repo>" or "<repo>:<plugin>" for audits.
    Manifest entries win on a name collision, then an earlier repo over a
    later one; the loser is skipped and surfaced in `warnings`.
    """
    entries: list[tuple[str, Path, Path]] = []
    warnings: list[str] = []
    missing: list[Path] = []
    discovered: set[tuple[str, str]] = set()
    origins: dict[Path, str] = {}
    claimed = set(taken_dsts)
    for spec in manifest.get("skill_repos", []):
        if isinstance(spec, str):
            spec = {"path": spec}
        repo = expand_path(spec["path"])
        if not repo.is_dir():
            missing.append(repo)
            continue
        dirs, mkt_name, w = repo_skill_dirs(repo, spec.get("plugins"))
        warnings.extend(w)
        for d, plugin in dirs:
            if mkt_name and plugin:
                discovered.add((mkt_name, plugin))
            dst = skills_target / d.name
            if dst in claimed:
                warnings.append(f"{repo.name}/{d.name}: already defined at "
                                f"{dst}, skipped")
                continue
            claimed.add(dst)
            entries.append((d.name, d, dst))
            origins[dst] = f"{repo.name}:{plugin}" if plugin else repo.name
    return entries, warnings, missing, discovered, origins


def offer_claude(failures: list[str]) -> None:
    """If claude is on PATH, offer to run it with the failure context."""
    if not shutil.which("claude"):
        return
    if not sys.stdin.isatty():
        return
    lines = "\n".join(f"  - {f}" for f in failures)
    prompt = (
        f"The qbranch script failed with the following problems:\n"
        f"{lines}\n"
        f"Please help me fix them."
    )
    print(f"\nRun claude to fix this? [y/N] ", end="", flush=True)
    try:
        answer = input().strip().lower()
    except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):
        print()
        return
    if answer == "y":
        os.execvp("claude", ["claude", prompt])


def add_skill_to_manifest(
    manifest_name: str,
    skill_name: str,
    repo: str | None = None,
    skill_path: str | None = None,
) -> bool:
    """Add skill_name to manifest. Returns True if manifest was modified."""
    p = REPO / "manifests" / f"{manifest_name}.json"
    manifest = json.loads(p.read_text())
    existing = {e["name"] for e in manifest.get("skills", [])}
    if skill_name in existing:
        return False
    if repo:
        entry: dict = {
            "name": skill_name,
            "repo": repo,
            "path": skill_path or f"skills/{skill_name}",
        }
    else:
        entry = {
            "name": skill_name,
            "path": f"${{QBRANCH_ROOT}}/skills/{skill_name}",
        }
    manifest.setdefault("skills", []).append(entry)
    p.write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2) + "\n")
    return True


def remove_skill_from_manifest(manifest_name: str, skill_name: str) -> bool:
    """Remove skill_name from manifest. Returns True if manifest was modified."""
    p = REPO / "manifests" / f"{manifest_name}.json"
    manifest = json.loads(p.read_text())
    before = manifest.get("skills", [])
    after = [e for e in before if e.get("name") != skill_name]
    if len(after) == len(before):
        return False
    manifest["skills"] = after
    p.write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2) + "\n")
    return True


def merge_fragments(base: dict, overlay: dict) -> dict:
    """Merge a settings fragment onto base policy.

    Dicts merge recursively, lists union (base order first), scalars from
    the overlay win.
    """
    out = dict(base)
    for k, v in overlay.items():
        cur = out.get(k)
        if isinstance(cur, dict) and isinstance(v, dict):
            out[k] = merge_fragments(cur, v)
        elif isinstance(cur, list) and isinstance(v, list):
            out[k] = cur + [i for i in v if i not in cur]
        else:
            out[k] = deepcopy(v)
    return out


def assert_settings(live: dict, policy: dict) -> None:
    """Impose policy onto live settings in place.

    Policy scalars overwrite, policy list items are appended if missing
    (app-added items are kept), dicts recurse. Keys the policy doesn't
    mention are left alone — they belong to the app.
    """
    for k, v in policy.items():
        cur = live.get(k)
        if isinstance(v, dict) and isinstance(cur, dict):
            assert_settings(cur, v)
        elif isinstance(v, list) and isinstance(cur, list):
            for item in v:
                if item not in cur:
                    cur.append(deepcopy(item))
        else:
            live[k] = deepcopy(v)


def retract_settings(live: dict, old: dict, new: dict) -> None:
    """Remove what the old policy asserted but the new one no longer does.

    List items are removed exactly; scalars only if the live value still
    equals what old policy set (a locally changed value is app state now);
    dicts recurse and are pruned when emptied.
    """
    for k, old_v in old.items():
        if k not in live:
            continue
        live_v = live[k]
        new_v = new.get(k)
        if isinstance(old_v, dict) and isinstance(live_v, dict):
            retract_settings(live_v, old_v,
                             new_v if isinstance(new_v, dict) else {})
            if not live_v and not isinstance(new_v, dict):
                del live[k]
        elif isinstance(old_v, list) and isinstance(live_v, list):
            new_items = new_v if isinstance(new_v, list) else []
            gone = [i for i in old_v if i not in new_items]
            live[k] = [i for i in live_v if i not in gone]
            if not live[k] and not new_items:
                del live[k]
        elif k not in new and live_v == old_v:
            del live[k]


def load_fragments(raw_paths: list[str]) -> tuple[list[tuple[Path, dict]], list[str]]:
    """Read settings fragments in manifest order. Returns (loaded, failures)."""
    loaded: list[tuple[Path, dict]] = []
    failures: list[str] = []
    for raw in raw_paths:
        p = expand_path(raw)
        if not p.is_file():
            failures.append(f"settings fragment missing: {p}")
            continue
        try:
            loaded.append((p, json.loads(p.read_text())))
        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
            failures.append(f"settings fragment unparseable: {p}: {e}")
    return loaded, failures


def sync_settings(
    agent: str, manifest_key: str, target: Path, state_key: str,
    manifest: dict, state: dict, dry_run: bool
) -> tuple[list[str], dict | None, list[str]]:
    """Merge `manifest_key` fragments into the app-owned settings file `target`.

    The live file is never symlinked: the app owns it and freely rewrites
    it (theme, effortLevel, plugins, ...). This asserts the policy keys
    from the fragments into it and retracts whatever the previous sync's
    policy asserted that the current one no longer does. The applied
    policy snapshot is returned for the state file under `state_key`.

    Returns (notes, applied_policy_or_None, failures).
    """
    notes: list[str] = []
    failures: list[str] = []
    fragments = manifest.get(manifest_key, [])
    old_applied = state.get(state_key) or {}

    loaded, load_failures = load_fragments(fragments)
    if load_failures:
        failures.extend(load_failures)
        return notes, None, failures
    policy: dict = {}
    for _, frag in loaded:
        policy = merge_fragments(policy, frag)

    if not fragments and not old_applied:
        return notes, {}, failures

    if target.is_symlink():
        # Legacy layout: the live file was a symlink into the repo. Capture
        # its content into a real, app-owned file before merging into it.
        content = target.resolve().read_text() if target.exists() else "{}\n"
        notes.append(f"{agent} settings: converting symlink -> real file  {target}")
        if not dry_run:
            target.unlink()
            target.write_text(content)
        live = json.loads(content)
    elif target.is_file():
        try:
            live = json.loads(target.read_text())
        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
            failures.append(f"live settings unparseable, leaving alone: {target}: {e}")
            return notes, None, failures
    else:
        live = {}

    before = json.dumps(live, sort_keys=True)
    retract_settings(live, old_applied, policy)
    assert_settings(live, policy)
    if json.dumps(live, sort_keys=True) != before or not target.exists():
        verb = "would update" if dry_run else "updated"
        notes.append(f"{agent} settings: {verb} {target} "
                     f"from {len(fragments)} fragment(s)")
        if not dry_run:
            target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            target.write_text(json.dumps(live, indent=2) + "\n")
    else:
        notes.append(f"{agent} settings: {target} up to date "
                     f"({len(fragments)} fragment(s))")
    return notes, policy, failures


def claude_cli_json(*args: str) -> tuple[list | None, str]:
    """Run `claude <args> --json` and parse its output. Returns (data, error)."""
    cmd = ["claude", *args, "--json"]
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(
            cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
            timeout=120,
        )
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return None, f"{' '.join(cmd)}: {e}"
    if result.returncode != 0:
        detail = result.stderr.strip() or result.stdout.strip()
        return None, f"{' '.join(cmd)}: exit {result.returncode}: {detail}"
    try:
        return json.loads(result.stdout), ""
    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
        return None, f"{' '.join(cmd)}: unparseable output: {e}"


def marketplace_add_spec(entry: dict) -> str | None:
    """Turn an extraKnownMarketplaces entry into a `marketplace add` argument."""
    src = entry.get("source") or {}
    if src.get("source") == "github" and src.get("repo"):
        return src["repo"]
    return src.get("url") or src.get("path")


def plan_claude_plugins(
    policy: dict, old_policy: dict,
    discovered: set[tuple[str, str]] = frozenset(),
) -> tuple[list[tuple[str, str, list[str]]], list[str], list[str]]:
    """Plan the `claude plugin` calls that bring local plugins up to policy.

    `extraKnownMarketplaces` in the merged fragments names marketplaces to
    register; `enabledPlugins` entries set to true name plugins to install
    at user scope. Only additions are acted on. A plugin dropped from
    policy has already had its enabledPlugins entry retracted by the
    settings merge, and Claude Code treats an installed plugin with no
    entry as disabled (verified on 2.1.257: it lists as enabled=false), so
    it is reported rather than uninstalled — uninstalling also deletes the
    plugin's data directory, which is the user's call.

    Returns (actions, notes, failures); an action is (op, label, argv).
    """
    actions: list[tuple[str, str, list[str]]] = []
    notes: list[str] = []
    failures: list[str] = []

    want_mkts = dict(policy.get("extraKnownMarketplaces") or {})
    enabled = policy.get("enabledPlugins") or {}
    want = {pid for pid, on in enabled.items() if on is True}
    old_enabled = old_policy.get("enabledPlugins") or {}
    old_want = {pid for pid, on in old_enabled.items() if on is True}
    if not want_mkts and not want and not old_want:
        return actions, notes, failures
    if not shutil.which("claude"):
        notes.append("Claude Code plugins: skipped (claude not on PATH)")
        return actions, notes, failures

    known, err = claude_cli_json("plugin", "marketplace", "list")
    if err:
        failures.append(f"plugins: {err}")
        return actions, notes, failures
    installed, err = claude_cli_json("plugin", "list")
    if err:
        failures.append(f"plugins: {err}")
        return actions, notes, failures
    known_names = {m.get("name") for m in known}
    installed_ids = {p["id"] for p in installed if p.get("scope") == "user"}
    enabled_ids = {p["id"] for p in installed
                   if p.get("scope") == "user" and p.get("enabled")}

    # A plugin whose skills are already linked from a checkout would load
    # them a second time if it is also installed and enabled.
    twice = sorted(f"{plugin}@{mkt}" for mkt, plugin in discovered
                   if f"{plugin}@{mkt}" in enabled_ids)
    if twice:
        notes.append("double load: installed and enabled here while their "
                     "skills are also linked from a skill_repos checkout — "
                     "uninstall the plugin or narrow the repo's 'plugins' "
                     "list: " + ", ".join(twice))

    # The official marketplace is implied by any plugin that lives in it.
    if any(pid.endswith("@" + OFFICIAL_MARKETPLACE) for pid in want):
        want_mkts.setdefault(OFFICIAL_MARKETPLACE, OFFICIAL_MARKETPLACE_SOURCE)

    for name, entry in want_mkts.items():
        if name in known_names:
            continue
        spec = marketplace_add_spec(entry)
        if spec is None:
            failures.append(
                f"plugins: marketplace {name}: unsupported source {json.dumps(entry)}")
            continue
        actions.append(("add-mkt", name,
                        ["claude", "plugin", "marketplace", "add", spec]))

    for pid in sorted(want - installed_ids):
        mkt = pid.rpartition("@")[2] if "@" in pid else ""
        if mkt and mkt not in known_names and mkt not in want_mkts:
            failures.append(
                f"plugins: {pid}: marketplace '{mkt}' is not registered — "
                f"add it to extraKnownMarketplaces in a fragment")
            continue
        actions.append(("install", pid,
                        ["claude", "plugin", "install", pid, "--scope", "user"]))

    retracted = sorted((old_want - want) & installed_ids)
    if retracted:
        notes.append(
            "plugins no longer managed (dropped from the fragments; now "
            "disabled, still installed; `claude plugin uninstall <id>` to "
            "remove): " + ", ".join(retracted))
    unmanaged = sorted(installed_ids - set(enabled) - set(retracted))
    if unmanaged:
        notes.append("unmanaged plugins (installed here, declared in no "
                     "fragment): " + ", ".join(unmanaged))
    return actions, notes, failures


def plugin_marketplace_of(pid: str) -> str:
    return pid.rpartition("@")[2] if "@" in pid else ""


def host_fragment_of(fragments: list[str]) -> str | None:
    """The manifest's per-host fragment entry (raw, unexpanded), if any."""
    return next((r for r in fragments if "/settings/hosts/" in r), None)


def marketplace_entry_from_cli(m: dict | None) -> dict | None:
    """Rebuild an extraKnownMarketplaces entry from a `marketplace list` row."""
    if not m or not m.get("source"):
        return None
    src = {"source": m["source"]}
    for k in ("repo", "url", "path"):
        if m.get(k):
            src[k] = m[k]
    return {"source": src}


def plugin_status(
    manifest_name: str, manifest: dict, state: dict
) -> tuple[dict, list[str]]:
    """Classify this machine's user-scope plugins against the manifest.

    managed:   declared (true or false) by some fragment of the manifest
    unmanaged: installed here, declared nowhere
    dropped:   declared at the last sync, not any more, still installed

    Returns (report, failures). The report is what --plugin-status prints
    and what the review-plugins skill consumes.
    """
    fragments = manifest.get("claude_settings", [])
    report: dict = {
        "manifest": manifest_name,
        "base_fragment": str(expand_path(fragments[0])) if fragments else None,
        "host_fragment": None,
        "managed": {},
        "unmanaged": [],
        "dropped": [],
    }
    host_raw = host_fragment_of(fragments)
    if host_raw:
        report["host_fragment"] = str(expand_path(host_raw))
    loaded, failures = load_fragments(fragments)
    if failures:
        return report, failures

    declared: dict[str, dict] = {}
    declared_mkts: set[str] = {OFFICIAL_MARKETPLACE}
    for p, frag in loaded:
        for pid, val in (frag.get("enabledPlugins") or {}).items():
            declared[pid] = {"value": val, "fragment": str(p)}
        declared_mkts.update((frag.get("extraKnownMarketplaces") or {}).keys())

    if not shutil.which("claude"):
        return report, ["claude not on PATH — cannot read installed plugins"]
    known, err = claude_cli_json("plugin", "marketplace", "list")
    if err:
        return report, [err]
    installed, err = claude_cli_json("plugin", "list")
    if err:
        return report, [err]
    mkt_by_name = {m.get("name"): m for m in known}
    live = {p["id"]: p for p in installed if p.get("scope") == "user"}
    old_policy = state.get("claude_settings_applied") or {}
    old_want = {pid for pid, on in (old_policy.get("enabledPlugins") or {}).items()
                if on is True}

    for pid, info in declared.items():
        row = live.get(pid)
        report["managed"][pid] = {
            **info,
            "installed": row is not None,
            "enabled": bool(row and row.get("enabled")),
        }
    for pid, row in sorted(live.items()):
        if pid in declared:
            continue
        mkt = plugin_marketplace_of(pid)
        entry = {
            "id": pid,
            "version": row.get("version"),
            "enabled": bool(row.get("enabled")),
            "marketplace": mkt,
            "marketplace_declared": mkt in declared_mkts,
            "marketplace_source": marketplace_entry_from_cli(mkt_by_name.get(mkt)),
        }
        report["dropped" if pid in old_want else "unmanaged"].append(entry)
    return report, []


def print_plugin_status(report: dict) -> None:
    print(f"manifest: {report['manifest']}")
    print(f"base fragment: {report['base_fragment']}")
    host = report["host_fragment"]
    print(f"host fragment: {host or '(none — --manage-plugin --in host creates one)'}")
    managed = report["managed"]
    print(f"\nmanaged ({len(managed)}):")
    for pid, info in sorted(managed.items()):
        state = "installed" if info["installed"] else "NOT INSTALLED"
        on = "enabled" if info["enabled"] else "disabled"
        print(f"  {pid:<48} {json.dumps(info['value']):<6} {state}, {on}"
              f"  [{Path(info['fragment']).name}]")
    for key, title in (("unmanaged", "unmanaged (installed here, declared in no fragment)"),
                       ("dropped", "no longer managed (dropped from the fragments, still installed)")):
        rows = report[key]
        print(f"\n{title} ({len(rows)}):")
        for e in rows:
            on = "enabled" if e["enabled"] else "disabled"
            mkt = e["marketplace"] + ("" if e["marketplace_declared"] else " (marketplace undeclared)")
            print(f"  {e['id']:<48} v{e['version']}  {on}  {mkt}")


def manage_plugin(
    manifest_name: str, pid: str, where: str, value: bool
) -> tuple[list[str], list[str]]:
    """Declare pid in the manifest's base or host fragment.

    `where` is "base" (first fragment — every machine using it) or "host"
    (the manifest's hosts/ fragment, created and wired into the manifest if
    missing). A true value for a plugin from a non-official marketplace
    also declares that marketplace, so other machines can install it.
    Returns (notes, failures).
    """
    notes: list[str] = []
    failures: list[str] = []
    mpath = REPO / "manifests" / f"{manifest_name}.json"
    if not mpath.is_file():
        return notes, [f"manifest not found: {mpath}"]
    manifest = json.loads(mpath.read_text())
    fragments = list(manifest.get("claude_settings", []))
    if not fragments:
        return notes, [f"manifest {manifest_name} lists no claude_settings fragments"]

    if where == "base":
        raw = fragments[0]
    else:
        raw = host_fragment_of(fragments)
        if raw is None:
            raw = f"${{QBRANCH_ROOT}}/claude-code/settings/hosts/{manifest_name}.json"
            fragments.append(raw)
            manifest["claude_settings"] = fragments
            mpath.write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2) + "\n")
            notes.append(f"added {raw} to manifest {manifest_name}")
    fpath = expand_path(raw)
    frag = json.loads(fpath.read_text()) if fpath.is_file() else {}
    others, load_failures = load_fragments([r for r in fragments if r != raw])
    failures.extend(load_failures)

    for p, other in others:
        if pid in (other.get("enabledPlugins") or {}):
            notes.append(f"note: {pid} is also declared in {p} as "
                         f"{json.dumps(other['enabledPlugins'][pid])}; "
                         f"later fragments win")

    frag.setdefault("enabledPlugins", {})[pid] = value
    mkt = plugin_marketplace_of(pid)
    if value and mkt and mkt != OFFICIAL_MARKETPLACE:
        declared = mkt in (frag.get("extraKnownMarketplaces") or {}) or any(
            mkt in (other.get("extraKnownMarketplaces") or {}) for _, other in others)
        if not declared:
            known, err = ([], "claude not on PATH")
            if shutil.which("claude"):
                known, err = claude_cli_json("plugin", "marketplace", "list")
            row = next((m for m in (known or []) if m.get("name") == mkt), None)
            entry = marketplace_entry_from_cli(row)
            if entry:
                frag.setdefault("extraKnownMarketplaces", {})[mkt] = entry
                notes.append(f"declared marketplace {mkt} in {fpath.name}")
            else:
                failures.append(
                    f"marketplace {mkt} is not registered here"
                    f"{' (' + err + ')' if err else ''}; add it to "
                    f"extraKnownMarketplaces in {fpath} by hand")

    fpath.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fpath.write_text(json.dumps(frag, indent=2) + "\n")
    notes.append(f"{pid} = {json.dumps(value)} in {fpath}")
    return notes, failures


def frontmatter_description(skill_dir: Path) -> str:
    """The `description:` of a SKILL.md, folded scalars flattened; "" if none."""
    try:
        text = (skill_dir / "SKILL.md").read_text(errors="replace")
    except OSError:
        return ""
    if not text.startswith("---"):
        return ""
    end = text.find("\n---", 3)
    fm = text[3:end] if end != -1 else text[3:]
    out: list[str] = []
    grab = False
    for ln in fm.splitlines():
        if grab:
            if ln.startswith((" ", "\t")):
                out.append(ln.strip())
                continue
            break
        if ln.startswith("description:"):
            val = ln[len("description:"):].strip()
            if val in (">", ">-", ">+", "|", "|-", "|+"):
                grab = True
            else:
                out.append(val.strip("\"'"))
                break
    return " ".join(out)


def plugin_always_on_tokens(pid: str) -> int | None:
    """Parse `claude plugin details` for its always-on token estimate."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["claude", "plugin", "details", pid],
                           capture_output=True, text=True,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=60)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None
    m = re.search(r"Always-on:\s*~?([\d.,]+)\s*(k?)\s*tok", r.stdout)
    if not m:
        return None
    n = float(m.group(1).replace(",", ""))
    return int(n * 1000) if m.group(2) == "k" else int(n)


def audit(
    manifest_name: str, manifest: dict, state: dict, skills_target: Path
) -> tuple[dict, list[str]]:
    """Inventory the whole setup and flag what needs a human decision.

    Findings (each {kind, severity, message, items}):
      skill-collision          a name claimed by two skill sources
      plugin-skill-collision   a linked skill and an enabled plugin's skill share a name
      double-load              a plugin installed here whose skills are also linked
      mcp-duplicate            a user-scope MCP server an enabled plugin also provides
      unmanaged-plugins / dropped-plugins / disabled-plugins
      unlinked-repo-skills     skills in this repo the manifest does not link
      missing-skill-repos      skill_repos checkouts that are absent
      context-budget           counts and always-loaded token estimates
    Returns (report, failures).
    """
    failures: list[str] = []
    findings: list[dict] = []
    claude_ok, agy_ok = claude_installed(), agy_installed()

    desired, _ = collect_desired(manifest, skills_target, claude_ok, agy_ok)
    taken = {dst for _, _, dst in desired}
    repo_entries, repo_warnings, missing_repos, discovered, origins = (
        collect_repo_skills(manifest, skills_target, taken))
    skills: list[dict] = []
    for _, src, dst in desired + repo_entries:
        if dst.parent != skills_target or not (src / "SKILL.md").is_file():
            continue
        desc = frontmatter_description(src)
        skills.append({"name": dst.name, "path": str(src),
                       "origin": origins.get(dst, "manifest"),
                       "description_chars": len(desc)})
    if repo_warnings:
        findings.append({"kind": "skill-collision", "severity": "warn",
                         "message": "a skill name claimed by more than one "
                                    "source; the first listed source wins",
                         "items": repo_warnings})
    linked_srcs = {expand_path(e["path"]).resolve()
                   for e in manifest.get("skills", []) if "repo" not in e}
    unlinked = sorted(c.name for c in scan_skill_dirs(REPO / "skills")
                      if c.resolve() not in linked_srcs)
    if unlinked:
        findings.append({"kind": "unlinked-repo-skills", "severity": "info",
                         "message": "skills in this repo that the manifest "
                                    "does not link (--add-skill to link)",
                         "items": unlinked})
    if missing_repos:
        findings.append({"kind": "missing-skill-repos", "severity": "warn",
                         "message": "skill_repos checkouts not present here",
                         "items": [str(p) for p in missing_repos]})

    plugins: dict = {}
    user_mcp: dict = {}
    plugin_mcp: dict[str, dict] = {}
    plugin_costs: dict[str, int | None] = {}
    if claude_ok and shutil.which("claude"):
        pstatus, pfails = plugin_status(manifest_name, manifest, state)
        failures.extend(pfails)
        installed, err = claude_cli_json("plugin", "list")
        if err:
            failures.append(err)
            installed = []
        user_rows = [p for p in installed if p.get("scope") == "user"]
        enabled_rows = [p for p in user_rows if p.get("enabled")]
        plugin_skills: dict[str, list[str]] = {}
        for p in enabled_rows:
            pid = p["id"]
            plugin_costs[pid] = plugin_always_on_tokens(pid)
            plugin_skills[pid] = [d.name for d in scan_skill_dirs(
                Path(p.get("installPath") or "/nonexistent") / "skills")]
            if p.get("mcpServers"):
                plugin_mcp[pid] = p["mcpServers"]
        linked_names = {s["name"] for s in skills}
        overlap = [f"{n} (linked) vs {n} in {pid}"
                   for pid, names in plugin_skills.items()
                   for n in names if n in linked_names]
        if overlap:
            findings.append({"kind": "plugin-skill-collision", "severity": "warn",
                             "message": "a linked skill and an enabled plugin "
                                        "ship a skill of the same name",
                             "items": overlap})
        enabled_ids = {p["id"] for p in enabled_rows}
        twice = sorted(f"{pl}@{m}" for m, pl in discovered
                       if f"{pl}@{m}" in enabled_ids)
        if twice:
            findings.append({"kind": "double-load", "severity": "warn",
                             "message": "enabled plugins whose skills are also "
                                        "linked from a skill_repos checkout",
                             "items": twice})
        for key, sev, msg in (
            ("unmanaged", "info", "installed here, declared in no fragment — "
                                  "the review-plugins skill triages these"),
            ("dropped", "info", "dropped from the fragments, still installed"),
        ):
            if pstatus.get(key):
                findings.append({"kind": f"{key}-plugins", "severity": sev,
                                 "message": msg,
                                 "items": [e["id"] for e in pstatus[key]]})
        disabled = sorted(p["id"] for p in user_rows if not p.get("enabled"))
        if disabled:
            findings.append({"kind": "disabled-plugins", "severity": "info",
                             "message": "installed but disabled here; uninstall "
                                        "candidates if that is true everywhere",
                             "items": disabled})
        if CLAUDE_JSON_FILE.is_file():
            try:
                user_mcp = json.loads(CLAUDE_JSON_FILE.read_text()).get("mcpServers") or {}
            except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):
                pass

        def endpoint(cfg: dict) -> str:
            if cfg.get("url"):
                return cfg["url"].rstrip("/")
            return " ".join([cfg.get("command", "")] + list(cfg.get("args") or [])).strip()

        dup = []
        for name, cfg in user_mcp.items():
            for pid, servers in plugin_mcp.items():
                for sname, scfg in servers.items():
                    if endpoint(cfg) and endpoint(cfg) == endpoint(scfg):
                        dup.append(f"{name} (user scope) = {sname} in {pid}")
        if dup:
            findings.append({"kind": "mcp-duplicate", "severity": "warn",
                             "message": "user-scope MCP servers that an enabled "
                                        "plugin also provides; `claude mcp remove "
                                        "<name> -s user` drops the duplicate",
                             "items": dup})
        plugins = {
            "managed": sorted(pstatus.get("managed", {})),
            "enabled": sorted(enabled_ids),
            "disabled": disabled,
            "skills": plugin_skills,
            "always_on_tokens": plugin_costs,
        }

    desc_chars = sum(s["description_chars"] for s in skills)
    plugin_tokens = sum(v for v in plugin_costs.values() if v)
    largest = sorted(skills, key=lambda s: s["description_chars"], reverse=True)[:8]
    budget = {
        "skills": len(skills),
        "description_chars": desc_chars,
        "description_tokens_est": desc_chars // 4,
        "plugin_always_on_tokens": plugin_tokens,
        "largest_descriptions": [
            {"name": s["name"], "chars": s["description_chars"]} for s in largest],
    }
    findings.append({
        "kind": "context-budget", "severity": "info",
        "message": (f"{len(skills)} skills linked, ~{desc_chars // 4} tokens of "
                    f"always-loaded descriptions, ~{plugin_tokens} always-on "
                    f"tokens from {len(plugin_costs)} enabled plugins"),
        "items": [f"{s['name']}: {s['description_chars']} chars" for s in largest],
    })
    report = {
        "tool": VERSION, "manifest": manifest_name,
        "skills": skills, "plugins": plugins,
        "mcp": {"user_servers": sorted(user_mcp),
                "plugin_servers": {pid: sorted(s) for pid, s in plugin_mcp.items()}},
        "budget": budget, "findings": findings,
    }
    return report, failures


def print_audit(report: dict) -> None:
    b = report["budget"]
    print(f"manifest: {report['manifest']}   qbranch {report['tool']}")
    print(f"skills linked: {b['skills']}   description text: {b['description_chars']} "
          f"chars (~{b['description_tokens_est']} tok, always loaded)")
    p = report.get("plugins") or {}
    if p:
        print(f"plugins: {len(p['enabled'])} enabled, {len(p['disabled'])} disabled, "
              f"{len(p['managed'])} managed; always-on ~{b['plugin_always_on_tokens']} tok")
    m = report["mcp"]
    print(f"mcp: {len(m['user_servers'])} user-scope servers, "
          f"{sum(len(v) for v in m['plugin_servers'].values())} from plugins")
    for f in report["findings"]:
        print(f"\n[{f['severity']}] {f['kind']}: {f['message']}")
        for item in f["items"]:
            print(f"  - {item}")


def run_plugin_action(argv: list[str]) -> str | None:
    """Run one planned `claude plugin` call. Returns an error message or None."""
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(
            argv, capture_output=True, text=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
            timeout=600,
        )
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return str(e)
    if result.returncode == 0:
        return None
    lines = (result.stderr.strip() or result.stdout.strip()).splitlines()
    return " ".join(lines[-2:]) or f"exit {result.returncode}"


def migrate_skills_dir(dst: Path, src: Path, copying: bool) -> str | None:
    """Replace a real per-agent skills directory with a link to (or copy of) src.

    Stale symlinks inside have already been removed by the cleanup pass; the
    directory must be empty apart from a state file. Returns an error
    message, or None on success.
    """
    for junk in (dst / STATE_FILE_NAME, dst / LEGACY_STATE_FILE_NAME,
                 dst / ".DS_Store"):
        if junk.is_file():
            junk.unlink()
    try:
        dst.rmdir()
    except OSError:
        leftover = ", ".join(sorted(p.name for p in dst.iterdir()))
        return (f"{dst} is a directory and still contains: {leftover} — "
                f"move these aside and re-run")
    if copying:
        copy_path(src, dst)
    else:
        dst.symlink_to(src)
    return None


def main() -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description="Sync agent state from a manifest into the local filesystem.",
        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
    )
    ap.add_argument("--manifest", "-m",
                    help="Manifest name under manifests/ (without .json). "
                         "Default: the last synced one, else this host's name, "
                         "else 'default'.")
    ap.add_argument("--skills-target", "-t",
                    default=str(DEFAULT_SKILLS_TARGET),
                    help=f"Where 'skills' entries get linked "
                         f"(default: {DEFAULT_SKILLS_TARGET}). The state file "
                         f"also lives here.")
    ap.add_argument("--dry-run", "-n", action="store_true",
                    help="Print plan without changing the filesystem. With "
                         "--json, print the plan as JSON instead.")
    ap.add_argument("--root", metavar="DIR",
                    help="Config root holding manifests/, skills/ and "
                         "claude-code/. Default: $QBRANCH_ROOT, else the root "
                         "remembered by the last sync, else the current "
                         "directory.")
    ap.add_argument("--link-mode", choices=LINK_MODES,
                    help="How entries are materialised: symlink (the default "
                         "where links work), copy (copied and refreshed on "
                         "every sync, for filesystems or Windows setups without "
                         "symlinks), auto (symlink, falling back to copy on "
                         "Windows without Developer Mode). Remembered like "
                         "--root; auto forgets.")
    ap.add_argument("--list", action="store_true",
                    help="List available manifests and exit.")
    ap.add_argument("--add-skill", "-a", metavar="SKILL",
                    help="Add SKILL to the target manifest(s) and exit. "
                         "Path defaults to ${QBRANCH_ROOT}/skills/SKILL.")
    ap.add_argument("--remove-skill", "-r", metavar="SKILL",
                    help="Remove SKILL from the target manifest(s) and exit.")
    ap.add_argument("--repo", metavar="URL",
                    help="Git repo URL for the skill (used with --add-skill). "
                         "On sync, ~/src/<repo-name> is checked first; "
                         "otherwise the repo is cloned to ~/.agents/skill-repos/.")
    ap.add_argument("--skill-path", metavar="PATH",
                    help="Path within the repo (used with --add-skill --repo). "
                         "Defaults to skills/<skill-name>.")
    ap.add_argument("--all", dest="all_manifests", action="store_true",
                    help="With --add-skill/--remove-skill: apply to every manifest "
                         "in manifests/. Prints a reminder to sync each machine afterwards.")
    ap.add_argument("--version", action="version",
                    version=f"qbranch {VERSION} (manifest schema "
                            f"{MANIFEST_SCHEMA})")
    ap.add_argument("--skill", nargs="?", const="", metavar="NAME",
                    help="Print bundled skill NAME (its SKILL.md, verbatim) and "
                         "exit; without NAME, list the bundled skills. These "
                         "are the tool's own skills, review-plugins and "
                         "agent-audit, so an agent that finds qbranch on PATH "
                         "can read how to drive it.")
    ap.add_argument("--upgrade-manifests", action="store_true",
                    help="Rewrite every manifest under manifests/ at the "
                         "current schema and exit. Older manifests work "
                         "without this (they are upgraded in memory); a "
                         "manifest newer than this tool is refused.")
    ap.add_argument("--plugin-status", action="store_true",
                    help="Report this machine's Claude Code plugins as managed / "
                         "unmanaged / no longer managed against the target "
                         "manifest, and exit.")
    ap.add_argument("--audit", action="store_true",
                    help="Inventory skills, plugins and MCP servers on this "
                         "machine against the target manifest and report "
                         "collisions, double loads, duplicates, dead weight "
                         "and the context budget; then exit.")
    ap.add_argument("--json", action="store_true",
                    help="With --plugin-status or --audit: machine-readable output.")
    ap.add_argument("--manage-plugin", metavar="ID",
                    help="Declare plugin ID (name@marketplace) in a fragment of "
                         "the target manifest and exit. Needs --in; see --value.")
    ap.add_argument("--in", dest="fragment_kind", choices=["base", "host"],
                    help="With --manage-plugin: 'base' is the shared first "
                         "fragment (every machine using it); 'host' is this "
                         "manifest's hosts/ fragment, created and wired into the "
                         "manifest if missing.")
    ap.add_argument("--value", choices=["true", "false"], default="true",
                    help="With --manage-plugin: true installs and enables the "
                         "plugin wherever the fragment applies; false pins it "
                         "disabled there. Default: true.")
    args = ap.parse_args()

    if args.skill is not None:
        return print_skill(args.skill)

    skills_target = Path(args.skills_target).expanduser()
    state_path = skills_target / STATE_FILE_NAME

    if args.list:
        resolve_root(args.root, load_state(state_path))
        for n in list_manifests():
            print(n)
        return 0

    if args.upgrade_manifests:
        resolve_root(args.root, load_state(state_path))
        return upgrade_manifests()

    if args.plugin_status or args.manage_plugin or args.audit:
        state = load_state(state_path)
        resolve_root(args.root, state)
        manifest_name = choose_manifest(args.manifest, state)
        if args.audit:
            manifest, _ = load_manifest(manifest_name)
            report, fails = audit(manifest_name, manifest, state, skills_target)
            if args.json:
                print(json.dumps({**report, "errors": fails}, indent=2))
            else:
                print_audit(report)
                for f in fails:
                    print(f"ERROR: {f}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1 if fails else 0
        if args.manage_plugin:
            if not args.fragment_kind:
                sys.exit("--manage-plugin needs --in base|host")
            notes, fails = manage_plugin(
                manifest_name, args.manage_plugin, args.fragment_kind,
                args.value == "true")
            for n in notes:
                print(n)
            for f in fails:
                print(f"ERROR: {f}", file=sys.stderr)
            if not fails:
                print("Run qbranch to apply.")
            return 1 if fails else 0
        manifest, _ = load_manifest(manifest_name)
        report, fails = plugin_status(manifest_name, manifest, state)
        if args.json:
            print(json.dumps({**report, "errors": fails}, indent=2))
        else:
            print_plugin_status(report)
            for f in fails:
                print(f"ERROR: {f}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1 if fails else 0

    if args.add_skill and args.remove_skill:
        sys.exit("--add-skill and --remove-skill are mutually exclusive")

    if args.add_skill or args.remove_skill:
        state = load_state(state_path)
        resolve_root(args.root, state)
        return edit_skill(args, state)

    if args.json and not args.dry_run:
        sys.exit("--json on a sync needs --dry-run (it prints the plan); "
                 "--plugin-status and --audit have their own JSON reports")
    return sync(args, skills_target, state_path)


def edit_skill(args: argparse.Namespace, state: dict) -> int:
    """--add-skill / --remove-skill against one manifest or all of them."""
    adding = bool(args.add_skill)
    skill_name = args.add_skill if adding else args.remove_skill

    repo_url = args.repo
    skill_path_arg = args.skill_path

    if adding and skill_name.startswith("git://"):
        skill_name, repo_url, skill_path_arg = parse_git_skill_url(skill_name)

    if adding:
        if repo_url:
            local_root = Path.home() / "src" / repo_name_from_url(repo_url)
            if not local_root.is_dir():
                print(f"note: {local_root} not found — will clone on sync")
        else:
            skill_dir = REPO / "skills" / skill_name
            if not skill_dir.is_dir():
                print(f"error: {skill_dir} not found", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2

    add_kwargs = {}
    if adding and repo_url:
        add_kwargs["repo"] = repo_url
        add_kwargs["skill_path"] = skill_path_arg

    def apply(mname: str, sname: str) -> bool:
        if adding:
            return add_skill_to_manifest(mname, sname, **add_kwargs)
        return remove_skill_from_manifest(mname, sname)

    if args.all_manifests:
        targets = list_manifests()
        if not targets:
            sys.exit("no manifests found")
        for mname in targets:
            changed = apply(mname, skill_name)
            if adding:
                status = "added" if changed else "already present"
            else:
                status = "removed" if changed else "not present"
            print(f"  {status:<15}  {mname}")
        print(f"\nRemember to run qbranch on each machine to apply.")
        return 0

    manifest_name = choose_manifest(args.manifest, state)
    changed = apply(manifest_name, skill_name)
    if adding:
        verb, already = "added to", "already in"
    else:
        verb, already = "removed from", "not in"
    if changed:
        print(f"'{skill_name}' {verb} manifest '{manifest_name}'")
        print(f"Run qbranch to apply.")
    else:
        print(f"'{skill_name}' {already} manifest '{manifest_name}'")
    return 0


def sync(args: argparse.Namespace, skills_target: Path, state_path: Path) -> int:
    """Plan the sync, print it (text or JSON), apply it unless --dry-run."""
    messages: list[dict] = []

    def say(level: str, text: str) -> None:
        """Record a message for the plan; print it unless building JSON."""
        messages.append({"level": level, "text": text})
        if args.json:
            return
        if level == "error":
            print(f"ERROR: {text}", file=sys.stderr)
        elif level == "info":
            print(f"  {text}")
        else:
            print(f"{level}: {text}")

    if not args.dry_run:
        skills_target.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)

    state = load_state(state_path)
    resolve_root(args.root, state)
    manifest_name = choose_manifest(args.manifest, state)
    manifest, upgrade_notes = load_manifest(manifest_name)
    for n in upgrade_notes:
        say("note", f"manifest '{manifest_name}': {n} (in memory; run "
                    f"--upgrade-manifests to rewrite manifests/)")
    mode_notes: list[str] = []
    link_mode, remembered_mode = decide_link_mode(args.link_mode, state, mode_notes)
    for n in mode_notes:
        say("note", n)
    copying = link_mode == "copy"
    claude_ok = claude_installed()
    agy_ok = agy_installed()

    # (display name, manifest key, app-owned live file, state key, installed?)
    settings_agents = (
        ("Claude Code", "claude_settings", CLAUDE_SETTINGS_FILE,
         "claude_settings_applied", claude_ok),
        ("Antigravity", "agy_settings", AGY_SETTINGS_FILE,
         "agy_settings_applied", agy_ok),
    )

    # Settings run before link planning: converting a legacy settings.json
    # symlink into a real file must happen before the stale-link remove pass
    # evaluates what is and isn't a symlink.
    settings_notes: list[str] = []
    settings_failures: list[str] = []
    applied_policy: dict[str, dict | None] = {}
    for agent, mkey, target, skey, installed in settings_agents:
        if installed:
            notes, policy, fails = sync_settings(
                agent, mkey, target, skey, manifest, state, args.dry_run)
            settings_notes.extend(notes)
            settings_failures.extend(fails)
            applied_policy[skey] = policy
        elif manifest.get(mkey):
            settings_notes.append(f"{agent} settings: skipped (not installed)")

    desired, skipped = collect_desired(manifest, skills_target, claude_ok, agy_ok)
    taken_dsts = {dst for _, _, dst in desired}
    repo_entries, repo_warnings, missing_repos, discovered, _ = (
        collect_repo_skills(manifest, skills_target, taken_dsts))
    desired.extend(repo_entries)
    # A copy of the skills directory can only be made once everything in it
    # is there: the per-harness skills entries go last.
    desired = ([d for d in desired if d[1] != skills_target]
               + [d for d in desired if d[1] == skills_target])

    # Plugins follow the merged Claude policy: the settings pass has already
    # asserted the keys, this plans the CLI calls that make them true.
    plugin_actions: list[tuple[str, str, list[str]]] = []
    if claude_ok and applied_policy.get("claude_settings_applied") is not None:
        plugin_actions, plugin_notes, plugin_failures = plan_claude_plugins(
            applied_policy["claude_settings_applied"],
            state.get("claude_settings_applied") or {}, discovered)
        settings_notes.extend(plugin_notes)
        settings_failures.extend(plugin_failures)

    for repo in missing_repos:
        say("note", f"skill repo {repo} not found — clone it, or drop it "
                    f"from the manifest's skill_repos")
    for w in repo_warnings:
        say("warning", w)
    for s in skipped:
        say("skipped", s)
    for n in settings_notes:
        say("info", n)
    for f in settings_failures:
        say("error", f)

    desired_dsts = {dst for _, _, dst in desired}
    previous_dsts = {Path(p) for p in state.get("links", [])}
    previous_copies = {Path(p) for p in state.get("copies", [])}

    # The live settings.json is managed by the settings merge, not as a
    # link — keep the remove pass away from it even if an old state file
    # still lists it from the symlink era.
    managed: set[Path] = set()
    for _, mkey, target, _, installed in settings_agents:
        if installed and manifest.get(mkey):
            managed.add(target)

    actions: list[tuple[str, str, Path | None, Path, str]] = []

    for dst in sorted(previous_dsts - desired_dsts - managed):
        if dst.is_symlink():
            actions.append(("remove", dst.name, None, dst,
                            f"-> {dst.readlink()} (not in manifest)"))
        elif dst in previous_copies and dst.exists():
            actions.append(("remove", dst.name, None, dst, "copy (not in manifest)"))

    create = "copy" if copying else "link"
    for label, src, dst in desired:
        if not src.exists() and not (args.dry_run and src == skills_target):
            # A MISS never reaches `final`, so its dst never lands in the
            # state file — the stale-removal pass above (which walks
            # previous_dsts) can therefore never reclaim a symlink left
            # here, and it would dangle forever. Clear it as part of the
            # failure instead. Only a symlink whose target is gone is
            # touched; a working link is left for the WARN/relink paths.
            note = "source missing"
            if dst.is_symlink() and not dst.exists():
                note = "source missing (will remove stale link)"
            actions.append(("MISS", label, src, dst, note))
            continue
        if dst.is_symlink():
            cur_raw = Path(os.readlink(dst))
            cur = (dst.parent / cur_raw).resolve() if not cur_raw.is_absolute() else cur_raw.resolve()
            if cur == src.resolve():
                actions.append(("ok", label, src, dst, ""))
            elif copying:
                actions.append(("copy", label, src, dst, f"was: link -> {cur_raw}"))
            else:
                actions.append(("relink", label, src, dst, f"was: {cur_raw}"))
        elif dst in previous_copies and dst.exists():
            # A copy an earlier sync made: refresh it, or turn it back into
            # a link if the mode changed.
            if not copying:
                actions.append(("relink", label, src, dst, "was: copy"))
            elif copy_up_to_date(src, dst):
                actions.append(("ok", label, src, dst, "copy"))
            else:
                actions.append(("copy", label, src, dst, "refresh"))
        elif dst.is_dir() and dst in (CLAUDE_SKILLS_LINK, AGY_SKILLS_LINK):
            actions.append(("migrate", label, src, dst,
                            f"dir -> {'copy' if copying else 'symlink'} "
                            f"(after stale links removed)"))
        elif dst.exists():
            actions.append(("WARN", label, src, dst,
                            "non-symlink at destination — leaving alone"))
        else:
            actions.append((create, label, src, dst, ""))

    if not args.json:
        label_w = max(
            (len(label) for _, label, *_ in actions + plugin_actions), default=8)
        for op, label, src, dst, note in actions:
            srcs = f"{dst} -> {src}" if src else f"{dst}"
            print(f"  {op:<7} {label:<{label_w}}  {note}  {srcs}".rstrip())
        for op, label, argv in plugin_actions:
            print(f"  {op:<7} {label:<{label_w}}  {' '.join(argv)}")
        if not actions and not plugin_actions:
            print("  (nothing to do)")

    manifest_skill_srcs = {
        expand_path(e["path"]).resolve()
        for e in manifest.get("skills", [])
        if "repo" not in e
    }
    repo_skills = REPO / "skills"
    unsynced = sorted(
        child.name
        for child in (repo_skills.iterdir() if repo_skills.is_dir() else [])
        if child.is_dir() and child.resolve() not in manifest_skill_srcs
    )
    if unsynced:
        say("note", f"not in manifest: {', '.join(unsynced)}")

    if args.json:
        plan = {
            "tool": VERSION,
            "schema": MANIFEST_SCHEMA,
            "manifest": manifest_name,
            "dry_run": True,
            "skills_target": str(skills_target),
            "link_mode": link_mode,
            "claude": claude_ok,
            "agy": agy_ok,
            "desired": len(desired_dsts),
            "actions": [
                {"op": op, "label": label, "src": str(src) if src else None,
                 "dst": str(dst), "note": note}
                for op, label, src, dst, note in actions],
            "plugin_actions": [
                {"op": op, "label": label, "argv": argv}
                for op, label, argv in plugin_actions],
            "unlinked_repo_skills": unsynced,
            "messages": messages,
            "failures": settings_failures,
        }
        print(json.dumps(plan, indent=2))
        return 1 if settings_failures else 0

    print()
    print(f"manifest={manifest_name}  desired={len(desired_dsts)}  "
          f"skills_target={skills_target}  link_mode={link_mode}  "
          f"claude={'yes' if claude_ok else 'no'}  agy={'yes' if agy_ok else 'no'}")

    if args.dry_run:
        print("(dry run — no changes made)")
        return 1 if settings_failures else 0

    final: list[Path] = []
    copies: list[Path] = []
    had_error = bool(settings_failures)
    failures: list[str] = list(settings_failures)
    for op, label, src, dst, note in actions:
        try:
            if op == "remove":
                remove_path(dst)
            elif op == "relink":
                remove_path(dst)
                dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                dst.symlink_to(src)
                final.append(dst)
            elif op == "link":
                dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                dst.symlink_to(src)
                final.append(dst)
            elif op == "copy":
                copy_path(src, dst)
                final.append(dst)
                copies.append(dst)
            elif op == "ok":
                final.append(dst)
                if dst in previous_copies and not dst.is_symlink():
                    copies.append(dst)
            elif op == "migrate":
                msg = migrate_skills_dir(dst, src, copying)
                if msg:
                    print(f"ERROR: {label}: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
                    failures.append(f"{label}: {msg}")
                    had_error = True
                else:
                    final.append(dst)
                    if copying:
                        copies.append(dst)
            elif op == "WARN":
                msg = f"{label}: non-symlink at {dst} — refusing to overwrite"
                print(f"ERROR: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
                failures.append(msg)
                had_error = True
            elif op == "MISS":
                msg = f"{label}: source missing at {src}"
                if dst.is_symlink() and not dst.exists():
                    dst.unlink()
                    msg += f" (removed stale link at {dst})"
                print(f"ERROR: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
                failures.append(msg)
                had_error = True
        except OSError as e:
            msg = f"{label} ({dst}): {e}"
            print(f"ERROR: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
            failures.append(msg)
            had_error = True

    # Marketplaces come before the plugins that need them (planned in that
    # order). Each call may clone a repo, so show progress per item.
    for op, label, argv in plugin_actions:
        print(f"  {op:<7} {label} ...", end="", flush=True)
        err = run_plugin_action(argv)
        if err:
            print(" FAILED")
            msg = f"{label}: {' '.join(argv)}: {err}"
            print(f"ERROR: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
            failures.append(msg)
            had_error = True
        else:
            print(" done")

    for _, _, _, skey, _ in settings_agents:
        if applied_policy.get(skey) is None:
            # Settings failed or the agent is absent: keep the previous
            # snapshot so a future sync can still retract what an older
            # policy asserted.
            applied_policy[skey] = state.get(skey) or {}
    save_state(state_path, manifest_name, final, copies, remembered_mode,
               applied_policy)

    if failures:
        offer_claude(failures)

    return 1 if had_error else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main())
